://openlibrary.org/books/OL7280473M/Buddhism_Is_Not_What_You_Think","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL7280473M/Buddhism_Is_Not_What_You_Think","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/33127-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["HarperOne"],"identifiers":{"goodreads":["777"],"librarything":["7491403"]},"subtitle":"Finding Freedom Beyond Beliefs","covers":[33127],"lc_classifications":["BQ4570.F7"],"key":"/books/OL7280473M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL232536A","name":"Steve Hagen"}],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"source_records":["bwb:9780060730574","amazon:0060730579","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2021-09-14"],"title":"Buddhism Is Not What You Think","number_of_pages":272,"isbn_13":["9780060730574"],"isbn_10":["0060730579"],"publish_date":"September 7, 2004","works":[{"key":"/works/OL1938073W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"first_sentence":{"type":"/type/text","value":"IF YOU VISIT a Buddhist temple in Japan, you'll likely encounter two gigantic, fierce, demonlike figures standing at either side of the entrance."},"local_id":["urn:bwbsku:P7-CMH-568"],"latest_revision":10,"revision":10,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-29T13:35:46.876380"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2022-12-07T21:37:11.889929"}}},"ISBN:9780060507237":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780060507237","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL7277353M/Buddhism_Is_Not_What_You_Think","preview":"restricted","preview_url":"https://archive.org/details/buddhismisnotwha0000hage","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/26121-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["HarperSanFrancisco"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"identifiers":{"goodreads":["915419"],"librarything":["7491403"]},"subtitle":"Finding Freedom Beyond Beliefs","title":"Buddhism Is Not What You Think","number_of_pages":272,"covers":[26121],"isbn_13":["9780060507237"],"isbn_10":["0060507233"],"publish_date":"October 7, 2003","key":"/books/OL7277353M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL232536A","name":"Steve Hagen"}],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL1938073W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"first_sentence":{"type":"/type/text","value":"IF YOU VISIT a Buddhist temple in Japan, you'll likely encounter two gigantic, fierce, demonlike figures standing at either side of the entrance."},"lccn":["2003050812"],"lc_classifications":["BQ4570.F7 H34 2003","BQ4570.F7H34 2003"],"source_records":["marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part30.utf8:191020427:779","bwb:9780060507237","ia:buddhismisnotwha0000hage","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2022-03-17","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.09.20150123.full.mrc:205388088:731","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_006.bib.mrc:268206355:3364"],"ocaid":"buddhismisnotwha0000hage","local_id":["urn:bwbsku:O5-QDY-359"],"oclc_numbers":["52092101"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Renowned Zen teacher Steve Hagen penetrates the most essential and enduring questions at the heart of the Buddha's teachings: How can we see the world in each moment, rather than merely as what we think, hope, or fear it is? How can we base our actions on reality, rather than on the longing and loathing of our hearts and minds? How can we live lives that are wise, compassionate, and in tune with reality? And how can we separate the wisdom of Buddhism from the cultural trappings and misconceptions that have come to be associated with it? Drawing on down-to-earth examples from everyday life and stories from Buddhist teachers past and present, Hagen tackles these fundamental inquiries with lucid prose. The newcomer to Buddhism will be inspired by this accessible and provocative introduction, and those more familiar with Buddhism will welcome this much needed hands-on guide to understanding what it truly means to be awake.--From publisher description."},"latest_revision":12,"revision":12,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-29T13:35:46.876380"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-06-30T11